    "findings": [
      "IR3 represents byte values in half registers; conversions mask unsigned sources or sign extend signed sources. Low-eight-bit add/sub/multiply/bitwise operations preserve the required byte result.",
      "ir3_lower_bit_size widens byte signedness-sensitive min/max, abs/negate, shifts, comparisons and supporting operations; the common lower_bit_size pass is part of mandatory lowering.",
      "Byte division/remainder passes through existing nir_lower_idiv small-width legalization; private/internal float16 operations do not enable application Float16 capability.",
      "Packing/bitcast lowering handles uint32 to byte vectors; byte float conversions pass through supported half/full representations.",
      "Private and shared byte arrays retain natural one-byte type layout and use existing typed LDL/STL/LDP/STP support. Native and output verification must confirm these paths for this consumer.",
      "V1 byte OpBitCount was invalid for Vulkan1.0 and was not executed. V2 explicitly widens built-ins whose core SPIR-V width is32; ordinary byte arithmetic remains byte-typed. Signed remainder and abs inputs are bounded to avoid undefined language domains."
    ],
